From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (agent session)" <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:00:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] renderer/d3d11: HLSL shader set, compiled to DXBC at build
 time

Adds the bg_color, cell_bg and cell_text shaders, an FxcStep that compiles
them, real Pipeline objects, and a RenderPass.step that actually issues draws.

Compiled at build time rather than runtime so there is no dependency on the
d3dcompiler redistributable, mirroring how the Metal backend ships a prebuilt
metallib. fxc rather than dxc because D3D11 loads DXBC and dxc only emits
DXIL, which is D3D12-only (DESIGN.md). FxcStep locates fxc by scanning the
SDK's versioned bin directories, since it is not on PATH outside a developer
command prompt; FXC overrides.

Layout, verified rather than assumed
------------------------------------
GenericRenderer writes one byte layout for every backend, so a mismatch
between the Globals cbuffer and Uniforms is a wrong-field read, not a compile
error. Every field carries an explicit packoffset, and the compiled reflection
was checked against the Zig struct field by field: projection_matrix 0,
screen_size 64, cell_size 72, grid_size 80, grid_padding 96, padding_extend
112, min_contrast 116, cursor_pos 120, cursor_color 124, bg_color 128, bools
132. CellText reflects at stride 32 with members at 0/8/16/20/24/28, matching
@sizeOf(CellText) and the buffer's StructureByteStride.

Two things that differ from the GLSL and would have been silent if copied:

- `bools` is four separate BYTES here, not a bitmask. Porting the GLSL's
  `bools & USE_LINEAR_BLENDING` test verbatim would read the wrong flag.
- `Mat` stores columns, which matches HLSL's default column_major cbuffer
  packing, so mul(M, v) is the right order.

Guarding pow
------------
fxc /WX rejected pow() on a possibly-negative base in linearize/unlinearize.
That is a real defect and not just a pedantic warning: HLSL's lerp evaluates
both branches, so a NaN from the branch the cutoff does not select still
propagates rather than being discarded. The premultiplied paths divide by
alpha before calling these, so a zero-alpha pixel can reach them. Inputs are
now clamped non-negative.

Also binds Draw, PSSetConstantBuffers, VSSetShaderResources, CreateBlendState
and OMSetBlendState, which were all Reserved vtable stubs, plus ID3D11BlendState
and the blend descriptors. Blending is premultiplied-alpha (ONE / INV_SRC_ALPHA)
because every shader outputs premultiplied color.

Register assignment is by fixed convention - t0/t1 buffers, t2/t3 atlases,
b0 uniforms - so HLSL register numbers do not shift with how many bindings a
step happens to pass. A step whose pipeline has no shaders is skipped, which
is how the not-yet-ported image and bg_image pipelines stay harmless.

Status: builds, all six shaders compile, directx11 tests pass (72). It does
NOT yet put glyphs on screen - the hwnd-host harness still renders a uniform
background. Cause not yet identified; Shaders.init succeeds and logs no error,
and a viewport is set. The phase1_skeleton markers therefore stay, since
removing them would claim a working draw path that is not proven.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
